list.item:
Chen, Eugene (Yu-jen), Chinese Minister
                        for Foreign Affairs at Canton, 1926, 1931, at Hankow, 1927, and at Nanking,
                        December 1931–January 1932.

Rea, George Bronson, American editor and
                        publisher, Far Eastern Review, Shanghai;
                        counselor, “Manchoukuo” government.

Sun Fo (Ke), Dr., Son of Dr. Sun Yat-sen;
                        President, Executive Yuan (Premier), Chinese National Government, December
                        1931–January 1932.

Yen, Dr. W. W., Chinese Minister in
                        United States; Representative, League of Nations Council and Assembly;
                        Ambassador to the Soviet Union, December.

person.note:
Marshal, former Commander in Chief, Kuominchun (People’s Army), north China;
                    Member, State Council, Chinese National Government; Chinese Military Council,
                    March 6.

U. S. Chairman, Advisory Commission of Railway Experts to Russia, 1918;
                    President, Inter-Allied Technical Board to operate Chinese Eastern and Siberian
                    Railways, 1919.
